      "SYDNEY: Oh, I’m not having kids. Maybe I’ll adopt when I’m forty --\nVEE: Sydney, stop.",
      "NANCY: Sorry. I had to call in a sub and then my car broke down and I had to wait for triple A. So what was this stunt you pulled?\nSYDNEY: It was my stunt, Nancy.\nNANCY: Surprise, surprise.",
      "NANCY: Sydney acts out to get attention --\nVEE: Mom, stop --\nSYDNEY: We get it, Nancy. Vee: good. Sydney: bad. I asked Vee to film me and I didn’t tell her what I was gonna do. Just suspend me. Leave her out o…",
      "NANCY: You know what Sydney has that you don’t? A trust fund. She can afford to screw up. You can’t. And by the way, you’re grounded.\nVEE: But it’s the last Falcons game of the season and I’m covering it --\nNANCY: No, you’re not. You’ll be doing laundry tonight.\nNANCY: Maybe I should go to NYU. Let you change bedpans for a while.",
      "NANCY: ‘Cause eleven years of that has made one thing clear. There are two kinds of people: doctors and nurses. Doctors make orders and nurses foll…\nVEE: That’s why I’m going to medical school."
    ]
